UX-ANIM-001.verified:
Two real browser contexts against the same URL, one default and one launched with reducedMotion: 'reduce', reading getComputedStyle on #book-bar:
ANIM-001 default        : {"matches":false,"barTransition":"width 0.3s"}
ANIM-001 reduce         : {"matches":true,"barTransition":"none","spinnerAnimation":"0s"}
(matches is matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches, so the media query really did flip; the bar's 300ms slide is gone and the pre-existing spinner rule still holds)

UX-CONT-003.verified:
Live page with the queue GET answering zero items (see the disclosure note below):
CONT-003 empty queue    : {"childCount":1,"visible":true,"text":"Nothing queued yet. What you write above waits here until you want it."}
DISCLOSURE: the daemon's real /api/queued right now returns 2 stored items, so the empty branch cannot be reached from live data without deleting the user's queued prompts. That one GET response was substituted in the browser so the real loadQueued() would run its zero-item path; the DOM measured above is the DOM the real function produced. Nothing in the daemon or the stored queue was changed.

